WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.879
If you want to know about how the psychic
power Danny Torrance has in The Shining contributed

00:00:03.879 --> 00:00:07.250
to bringing together the seven members of
the Losers Club, then stick around to the

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:07.960
end of this video.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.670
Twenty-nineteen has been a very Stephen Kingful
year for movie fans.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:20.980
There was a Pet Sematary movie, there’s
an It sequel, and there’s a Dr. Sleep movie,

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.449
as well as an adaptation for In The Tall Grass.

00:00:23.449 --> 00:00:26.670
When Pet Sematary was coming out I made this
video where I talked about how Ellie Creed

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:31.000
has the Shine, the psychic clairvoyance that
Dick Halloran tells Danny Torrance about in

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.000
The Shining.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:39.280
“She called it ‘Shining’ and for a long
time I thought it was just the two of us that

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.300
had ‘the shine’ to us.”

00:00:40.309 --> 00:00:41.309
It wasn’t.

00:00:41.309 --> 00:00:45.899
In fact, I’d go so far to say that all Stephen
King characters have a little bit of shine

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:48.899
to them, it’s just that some have a stronger
case than others.

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:51.289
It seems to be especially prominent in children.

00:00:51.289 --> 00:00:54.170
So what about the kids from King’s 1986
novel, It?

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:56.180
Let’s look at some of the evidence.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.280
[EVIDENCE]

00:00:58.289 --> 00:01:01.699
When Halloran explains the properties of The
Shine to Danny Torrance, the first thing he

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:03.860
talks about is the psychic connection.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:08.040
“I can remember when I was a little boy,

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:15.200
my grandmother and I could hold
conversations entirely without ever opening our mouths.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:18.599
She called it Shining.”

00:01:18.599 --> 00:01:22.909
The members of the Losers Club seem to have
this ability without explicitly knowing it,

00:01:22.909 --> 00:01:26.639
like just before Stan’s encounter with It
when he has the idea that The Standpipe seems

00:01:26.639 --> 00:01:27.920
like it’s floating.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.490
“That was an odd thought.

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:33.020
He supposed it must have come from his own
head -- where else could a thought come from?

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.580
-- but it somehow did not seem like his own
thought at all.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.689
Another example is when Eddie breaks his arm.

00:01:37.689 --> 00:01:41.159
Eddie falls asleep and dreams that his friends
came to see him at the hospital, and his Mom

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:42.880
tries to tell them off in the waiting room.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.240
A similar encounter did occur in real life,
but on the lawn of the Derry Home Hospital,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.450
not the waiting room.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:52.200
When Eddie wakes up he somehow knows that
what his Mom said to his friends was real

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.689
and he’s upset with her for it.

00:01:53.689 --> 00:02:01.120
“It’s like I go to sleep and he shows
me things, but when I wake up, I can’t remember

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.120
everything.”

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:06.540
Another property of The Shine is the ability
to see past and future events.

00:02:06.549 --> 00:02:10.030
In The Shining, Tony shows Danny the dangers
that await him at The Overlook Hotel.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:17.900
“Just like they can see things that haven’t
happened yet, well, sometimes they can see

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.870
things that happened a long time ago.”

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:24.049
In It, Bill senses that something bad is going
to happen before the rock fight against The

00:02:24.049 --> 00:02:27.209
Bowers Gang, and before they open the fortune
cookies as adults.

00:02:27.209 --> 00:02:30.549
There are a couple of other examples where
they are able to anticipate future events,

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:33.099
as well as one notable example of seeing into
the past.

00:02:33.099 --> 00:02:36.739
Just like Danny is able to see the murders
that took place in the Overlook Hotel, Richie

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:40.129
and Mike are able to see an event that took
place in The Barrens millions of years ago

00:02:40.129 --> 00:02:42.130
during the smoke hole ritual.

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:45.920
Another ability that is implied about the
shine is the ability to sense someone else’s

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:46.920
feelings.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:49.680
“What about Room 237?

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.219
You’re scared of Room 237 aintcha?”

00:02:54.219 --> 00:02:57.519
This one might be a little bit harder to prove,
because as humans we are able to read each

00:02:57.519 --> 00:03:00.900
other’s emotions to some degree based on
how someone acts, but there are a couple of

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:04.650
instances where Bill is able to sense what
It is feeling without even being in the same

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:05.780
room as It.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:09.379
For example after the incident with the photo
album, Bill first gets the idea that It is

00:03:09.379 --> 00:03:13.249
scared of them, and he has this feeling again
after finding the death threat left on the

00:03:13.249 --> 00:03:14.650
fridge in the junkyard.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:18.430
“Ih-It’s scuh-scuh-hared of u-u-us, you
know,” he said.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.260
“I can fuh-feel th-that.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.579
I swear to Guh-God I c-c-can.”

00:03:22.579 --> 00:03:26.950
On that note, the fact that It is even afraid
of these kids at all, when It’s been alive

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:30.590
for millions of years and killed hundreds
of people, could speak to the fact that It

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:34.949
knows that the shine is strong with them and
realizes the danger that this poses it It

00:03:34.949 --> 00:03:37.180
-- which brings me to my next point.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:41.450
The final battle that the Losers have with
It, as both kids and adults is a telekinetic

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.870
showdown known as the Ritual of Chud.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:48.469
As a kid, Bill is knocked outside of his physical
body into a void known as the Macroverse,

00:03:48.469 --> 00:03:52.019
where he must take hold of It’s metaphysical
tongue in order to hurt it.

00:03:52.019 --> 00:03:56.400
As adults, Bill tries to do this again, but
misses his shot, so Richie joins in and mentally

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:01.439
grabs onto It, causing it immense pain to
the point where It begs Richie to let go.

00:04:01.439 --> 00:04:06.430
“(let me go! let me go and you can have
everything you’ve ever wanted—money, fame,

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:09.239
fortune, power—I can give you these things)”

00:04:09.239 --> 00:04:13.769
So the Losers can use this telekinetic energy
as a weapon; this power can cause physical

00:04:13.769 --> 00:04:15.129
damage to a person.

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:17.370
And we see the same thing happen in The Shining.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:21.280
In Chapter 11, Halloran is trying to gauge
how powerful Danny’s shine is, and asks

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.419
him to give a blast of thought as hard as
he can.

00:04:23.419 --> 00:04:26.249
King describes it as coming in like a Nolan
Ryan fastball.

00:04:26.249 --> 00:04:27.249
!!! HI, DICK !!!

00:04:27.249 --> 00:04:29.960
“Hallorann winced and jerked backward on
the seat.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:33.940
His teeth came together with a hard click,
drawing blood from his lower lip in a thin

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:34.940
trickle.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:38.710
His hands flew up involuntarily from his lap
to the level of his chest and then settled

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:39.710
back again.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:44.410
For a moment his eyelids fluttered limply,
with no conscious control, and Danny was frightened.

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:45.410
“Mr. Hallorann?

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.410
Dick?

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:47.410
Are you okay?”

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:50.539
“I don’t know,” Hallorann said, and
laughed weakly.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.140
“I honest to God don’t.

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:55.680
The same thing happens later in the book,
when Danny is in trouble and tries to call

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.479
out to Dick, who is in Florida, using the
shine.

00:04:58.479 --> 00:05:02.300
The reason Danny is in trouble is because
he and his father, Jack, are strong shiners,

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:06.680
so they are able to see the evil in the hotel;
they can see all the ghosts of the Overlook’s

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:07.680
past.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.860
But most people come to the Overlook and never
have an issue -- in the movie there hasn’t

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:13.100
been an incident in the last 10 years.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:19.100
“I don’t suppose they told you anything
in Denver about the tragedy we had up here

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.440
during the Winter of 1970?”

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:24.669
I mentioned before that most people who shine
tend to be kids, and in Derry, kids are the

00:05:24.669 --> 00:05:26.259
biggest targets of It.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:29.540
“People die or disappear 6 times the national
average.”

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:32.060
“And that’s just grown-ups.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:34.180
Kids are worse.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:35.729
Way, way worse.”

00:05:35.729 --> 00:05:39.229
Then there’s the fact that it seems to be
mostly kids who can see It or the effects

00:05:39.229 --> 00:05:42.389
of It, like the blood that comes out of the
drain that Beverly’s parents can’t see,

00:05:42.389 --> 00:05:45.860
but the rest of the Losers Club can, or the
blood that comes out of Georgie’s photo

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:48.990
album that his parents can’t see but he
and Richie can.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:52.099
There are a few adults who are able to see
It, but for the most part, it’s something

00:05:52.099 --> 00:05:55.759
that kids have to deal with on their own,
as exemplified by the skateboard kid that

00:05:55.759 --> 00:06:00.150
Bill meets, who is surprised that Bill believes
the story about Tommy Vicananza seeing a shark

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:01.150
fin in the canal.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:04.900
Like I said, I think everyone has some degree
of shine to them.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:09.050
Halloran says he tried shining to Mrs. Torrance
and she just jumped the tiniest bit.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:12.580
But maybe the reason that the seven members
of the Losers Club are so drawn to one another,

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:16.430
is not just that they are all bullied by Henry
Bowers, but rather that they all have a strong

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:20.379
shine to them, and whether they know it or
not, that’s the reason they all become close.

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:24.650
At one point in the novel there was another
kid they hung out with called Bradley Donovan,

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:28.310
but he ended up getting in an argument with
Ben after accusing Beverly of cheating at

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:29.310
the game they were playing.

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:31.460
He never comes back around after that.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:35.050
Maybe he was partially ashamed about what
happened, but I think that he just didn’t

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:38.050
fit in with the others because he didn’t
have a strong shine like they did.

00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:41.600
There’s even a moment where Beverly almost
seems to make this conclusion in her thoughts.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.479
“But after a moment’s hesitation, Beverly
did tell.

00:06:44.479 --> 00:06:48.580
Because somehow Stanley was different from
Bradley—he was there in a way Bradley had

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:49.580
not been.”

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:52.659
Before I throw it to the end cards, let me
leave you with one more thought.

00:06:52.659 --> 00:06:57.110
The Shining and It share one common character,
and that is Dick Halloran, who is located

00:06:57.110 --> 00:07:01.419
in Derry in the year 1930 as a cook at The
Black Spot nightclub, but eventually leaves

00:07:01.419 --> 00:07:06.630
to become the head chef at the Overlook Hotel
in Colorado -- far away from Derry, Maine.

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:10.909
Could it be that because of It, Derry is just
about the scariest place in the world to live,

00:07:10.909 --> 00:07:14.850
because those who shine, like Dick, can see
the atrocities that occurred there on a daily

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:15.850
basis?

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:17.580
Let me know your thoughts on all that in the
comments.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:21.800
There’s more you have to know about the
shine, so watch my theory on how another Stephen

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:25.620
King character, Ellie Creed, also has a strong
case of it by hitting the video on the left.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:29.930
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring that deathbell for

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:32.770
notifications and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:35.120
Assuming we both survive.

